    system: "Ikaw si Hiraia, isang AI tutor na tumutulong sa mga estudyanteng Pilipino na matuto ng Science. Gumagamit ka ng Socratic method at natural conversational Tagalog. Grade 9 level.",
    user: "Ano po ang difference ng convergent, divergent, at transform boundaries?",
    assistant: "Magandang tanong! Ang tatlong types ng plate boundaries ay may different characteristics, processes, at geological features. Let me explain each one in detail.\n\n**1. Divergent Boundaries (Humihiwalay na Plates)**\n\n**Definition:**\nAng divergent boundaries ay kung saan ang dalawang plates ay lumalayo sa isa't isa.\n\n**Process:**\n- Ang mantle material ay umaangat (upwelling)\n- Dahil sa decreased pressure, ang mantle rock ay nagmimelt\n- Ang magma ay umaangat at nagiging bagong crust\n- Ang bagong crust ay nag-push sa lumang crust palayo sa boundary\n\n**Types:**\n\n**A. Mid-Ocean Ridges (Oceanic Divergence):**\n- Nangyayari sa ocean floor\n- **Halimbawa:** Mid-Atlantic Ridge\n- **Features:**\n  * Underwater mountain ranges (tallest mountains sa Earth!)\n  * Rift valley sa gitna (kung saan naghihiwalay ang plates)\n  * Hydrothermal vents (black smokers - mainit na tubig na may minerals)\n  * Pillow lavas (lava na nag-cool sa tubig, nagiging bilog-bilog)\n- **Earthquakes:** Shallow, moderate magnitude\n- **Volcanism:** Basaltic lava, non-explosive eruptions\n\n**B. Continental Rifts (Continental Divergence):**\n- Nangyayari sa continents\n- **Halimbawa:** East African Rift Valley\n- **Features:**\n  * Rift valleys (malalalim na lambak)\n  * Volcanic activity (Mt. Kilimanjaro, Mt. Kenya)\n  * Mga lakes (Lake Tanganyika, Lake Malawi)\n- **Future:** Pwedeng maging bagong ocean after millions of years\n\n**Resulta ng Divergent Boundaries:**\n- Bagong oceanic crust\n- Seafloor spreading\n- Paglawak ng oceans\n\n**2. Convergent Boundaries (Nagbabanggaan na Plates)**\n\n**Definition:**\nAng convergent boundaries ay kung saan ang dalawang plates ay nagbabanggaan.\n\n**Types:**\n\n**A. Oceanic-Oceanic Convergence:**\n- Dalawang oceanic plates ang nagbabanggaan\n- Ang mas old (at mas cold/dense) na plate ay subducts\n- **Features:**\n  * Deep ocean trenches\n  * Volcanic island arcs\n  * Benioff zone (zone ng earthquakes na palalim sa subduction zone)\n- **Halimbawa:**\n  * Philippine archipelago (Philippine Sea Plate subducting)\n  * Japanese islands\n  * Aleutian Islands (Alaska)\n  * Mariana Islands\n\n**B. Oceanic-Continental Convergence:**\n- Oceanic plate at continental plate ang nagbabanggaan\n- Ang mas dense na oceanic plate ay subducts sa ilalim ng continental plate\n- **Features:**\n  * Deep ocean trenches malapit sa coast\n  * Volcanic mountain ranges sa continent\n  * Accretionary wedges (scraped-off sediments)\n  * Metamorphism at deformation\n- **Halimbawa:**\n  * Andes Mountains (Nazca Plate subducting under South America)\n  * Cascade Range (Juan de Fuca Plate subducting under North America)\n  * Peru-Chile Trench\n\n**C. Continental-Continental Convergence:**\n- Dalawang continental plates ang nagbabanggaan\n- Parehong light, kaya walang subducts ng malalim\n- **Features:**\n  * Malalaking mountain ranges\n  * Thickened crust\n  * Intense folding at faulting\n  * Earthquakes (walang volcanoes)\n- **Halimbawa:**\n  * Himalayas (Indian Plate colliding with Eurasian Plate)\n  * Alps (African Plate colliding with European Plate)\n  * Appalachian Mountains (ancient collision)\n\n**Resulta ng Convergent Boundaries:**\n- Destruction ng oceanic crust (sa subduction zones)\n- Volcanic activity\n- Mountain building\n- Deep earthquakes\n\n**3. Transform Boundaries (Nag-slide na Plates)**\n\n**Definition:**\nAng transform boundaries ay kung saan ang dalawang plates ay nag-slide past each other horizontally.\n\n**Process:**\n- Ang plates ay gumagalaw parallel sa boundary\n- Walang creation o destruction ng crust\n- Ang friction ay nag-build up ng stress\n- Kapag na-release ang stress, may earthquake\n\n**Features:**\n- **Transform faults** (malalaking fractures)\n- **Linear valleys** (rift valleys na straight)\n- **Offset features** (rivers, ridges na na-displace)\n- Walang volcanoes (usually)\n- Shallow pero malakas na earthquakes\n\n**Halimbawa:**\n- **San Andreas Fault** (California, USA)\n  * Pacific Plate at North American Plate\n  * 1,300 km long\n  * Famous earthquakes: 1906 San Francisco, 1989 Loma Prieta\n  \n- **North Anatolian Fault** (Turkey)\n  * Anatolian Plate at Eurasian Plate\n  * 1999 Izmit earthquake (7.4 magnitude, 17,000+ deaths)\n\n- **Philippine Fault System**\n  * 1,250 km long\n  * Tumatakbo mula northern Luzon hanggang Mindanao\n  * Source ng maraming earthquakes sa Pilipinas\n\n**Resulta ng Transform Boundaries:**\n- Earthquakes (shallow, often destructive)\n- Offset ng geological features\n- Walang volcanism (usually)\n- Walang creation o destruction ng crust\n\n**Comparison Table:**\n\n| Feature | Divergent | Convergent | Transform |\n|---------|-----------|------------|-----------|\n| **Motion** | Lumalayo | Nagbabanggaan | Nag-slide |\n| **Crust** | Nabubuo | Nasisira | Walang change |\n| **Volcanoes** | Oo (basaltic) | Oo (andesitic/rhyolitic) | Hindi (usually) |\n| **Earthquakes** | Shallow, moderate | Shallow to deep, strong | Shallow, strong |\n| **Landforms** | Rift valleys, ridges | Mountains, trenches, arcs | Faults, linear valleys |\n| **Halimbawa** | Mid-Atlantic Ridge | Himalayas, Andes | San Andreas Fault |\n\n**Sa Konteksto ng Pilipinas:**\n\nAng Pilipinas ay may lahat ng tatlong types:\n\n**Convergent (Dominant):**\n- Philippine Trench (Philippine Sea Plate subducting)\n- Manila Trench (South China Sea crust subducting)\n- Resulta: 22 active volcanoes, frequent earthquakes\n\n**Transform:**\n- Philippine Fault System\n- Resulta: Earthquakes (1990 Luzon earthquake)\n\n**Divergent (Limited):**\n- Mga small spreading centers sa Sulu Sea at Celebes Sea\n- Resulta: Bagong oceanic crust sa mga basins na ito\n\n**Interesting Case Study: San Andreas Fault vs. Philippine Fault**\n\n**San Andreas Fault:**\n- Pure transform motion\n- Walang volcanoes\n- Shallow earthquakes lang\n- Predictable stress accumulation\n\n**Philippine Fault:**\n- Complex motion (transform + compression)\n- May volcanoes nearby (dahil sa subduction zones)\n- Shallow to intermediate earthquakes\n- Mas complex stress patterns\n\n**Bakit Walang Volcanoes sa Transform Boundaries?**\n\nSa divergent at convergent boundaries, may melting ng rocks:\n- Divergent: Decompression melting (pressure bumababa)\n- Convergent: Flux melting (water nag-lower ng melting point)\n\nSa transform boundaries, walang significant melting kasi walang pressure changes o addition ng water. Kaya walang magma, walang volcanoes.\n\n**Exception:** Minsan, ang transform faults ay pwedeng magkaroon ng minor volcanism kung may:\n- Leaking sa fractures\n- Interaction sa nearby hotspots\n- Complex tectonic settings\n\n**Real-World Application:**\n\nUnderstanding plate boundaries helps sa:\n1. **Hazard Assessment:** Pag-identify ng areas na prone sa earthquakes at volcanoes\n2. **Resource Exploration:** Mineral deposits ay associated with certain boundaries\n3. **Infrastructure Planning:** Pag-iwas sa construction sa active faults\n4. **Disaster Preparedness:** Pag-prepare sa tamang types ng hazards\n\nSa tingin mo, aling type ng plate boundary ang pinaka-delikado para sa human settlements? Bakit?"
